Z||000012||AusFiero||07-24-2001||05:33 AM||||Stay tuned for LT1 Chop Tops new wheel.<BR>He purchased it today. I will let him give you a look at it at his leisure. He can also tell you the price etc if he pleases. All I will say is you aint seen nothing like it  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Actually I only posted again because Jake said adaptor plates.  I have an engineering firm make them for me. Can fit any steering wheel to a Fiero using a bosskit off a dead Fiero wheel. Cost of an adaptor? To you guys US$49 shipped and insured to your door to suit any wheel you may have. Canadians will cop abouut $10 in fees at their end. But if interest keeps up in them price will drop as making one off is dearer than if I go get a few to keep in stock. <P>The advantage of an adaptor? Well you dont need a steering wheel puller to to fit your new wheel. The wheel stays in the exact right GM location. You can choose any damn wheel you want and not be limited by a Fiero Boss Kit being available. <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/ausfiero1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A> | <A HREF="http://www.auto-alley.com" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Accessories</A>||202.139.20.3||reg||1
Z||000013||Stage-2GT||07-24-2001||07:31 AM||||  LT-1, Go to <A HREF="http://www.LTBMotorsports.com" TARGET=_blank>www.LTBMotorsports.com</A>  I got my Commando there, just like Grins. I paid $260 for everything including the hud adapter. Correspond directly with Louis.<P>S2GT <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"><P>------------------<BR>"If Hate Was Money, I Would Own The World"||||reg||12
